 199+ 1020              ; Stencil operations
 200+ 1020
 201+ 1020              ; The currently stored stencil value is kept.
 202+ 1020              FT_KEEP                     EQU 0x01
 203+ 1020              ; The stencil value is replaced with the reference value set with StencilFunc
 204+ 1020              FT_REPLACE                  EQU 0x02
 205+ 1020              ; The stencil value is increased by 1 if it is lower than the maximum value
 206+ 1020              FT_INCR                     EQU 0x03
 207+ 1020              ; The stencil value is decreased by 1 if it is higher than the minimum value
 208+ 1020              FT_DECR                     EQU 0x04
 209+ 1020              ; Bitwise inverts the current stencil buffer value
 210+ 1020              FT_INVERT                   EQU 0x05
 211+ 1020              ; Same as FT_INCR, but wraps it back to 0 as soon as the maximum value is exceeded
 212+ 1020              FT_INCR_WRAP                EQU 0x06 ; undocumented???
 213+ 1020              ; Same as FT_DECR, but wraps it to the maximum value if it ends up lower than 0
 214+ 1020              FT_DECR_WRAP                EQU 0x07 ; undocumented???
